        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Preventing ice dams on a Utah roof requires stopping interior heat from escaping into the attic and melting snow unevenly. Focus on sealing warm air leaks, upgrading attic insulation, clearing snow with a roof rake, and installing edge systems like\n\nUtah Heat Cable\nor Hotedge Roof Ice Melt\nto maintain clear drainage paths.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Utah Heat Cable",
            "link": "https://utheatcable.com/2020/11/solutions-for-ice-dams/"
          },
          {
            "text": "Hotedge Roof Ice Melt",
            "link": "https://hotedge.com/ice-dam-prevention-in-utah/"
          }
        ],
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "sealing warm air leaks, upgrading attic insulation, clearing snow with a roof rake, and installing edge systems like Utah Heat Cable or Hotedge Roof Ice Melt to maintain clear drainage paths"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Stop Attic Heat Loss"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Seal gaps around ceiling penetrations, chimneys, and attic hatches."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Add insulation to meet local Utah building code values."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ensure intake and exhaust vents keep the attic cold like the outdoor air."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          4,
          5,
          7,
          9
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Manage Snow and Ice Physically"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Pull fresh snow off the lower 3 to 4 feet of the roof using a long-handled roof rake after heavy storms."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Avoid chipping or hammering ice on shingles to prevent punctures and leaks\n."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Opinions are mixed on Reddit (r/Roofing\n\n) regarding aggressive scraping, with users warning that direct metal contact can tear up asphalt granules.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "r/Roofing",
                "link": "https://www.reddit.com/r/Roofing/comments/1in0774/how_best_to_prevent_ice_dam/"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          6,
          7
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Install Active De-Icing Systems"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Set up self-regulating heat tape or cables in zig-zag patterns along eaves and inside gutters."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Use specialized edge metal panel assemblies\nor accredited systems like HotEdge to efficiently channel melting water away."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "If immediate removal is needed, place calcium chloride filled-nylon socks vertically across the dam rather than using rock salt, which ruins landscaping and corrodes metal."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, tell me:"
